\label{def:pij}
Let $\boldsymbol{d}\in \mathbf{D}_{\!R}$. For $(i,j)\in \sinterval{R}\times\sinterval{J}$, we write $\pcomp{i}{j}$ for the unique prime in $\mathcal{P}_j$ that divides $d_i$. Thus $\abs{d_i} = \prod_{j\in \sinterval{J}} \pcomp{i}{j}$.

For any subset ${I}\subset \sinterval{R}\times\sinterval{J}$, we set
\begin{equation*}
	\fprod{{\boldsymbol{d};I}} := \prod_{(i,j)\in {I}} \pcomp{i}{j}.
\end{equation*}
In the special case ${I} = \sinterval{R}\times\sinterval{J}$, we will write $\fprod{\boldsymbol{d}}$ instead of $\fprod{\boldsymbol{d};\sinterval{R}\times\sinterval{J}}$ to shorten notation.

By the triangle inequality,
\begin{equation*}
	\mathbb{E}\left[ \abs{ w_{\boldsymbol{d}}(\mathbf{n})   }\right] \leqslant \mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{i\in \sinterval{K}} \prod_{p\mid d_i} \abs{\ind{p\mid \mathbf{n} + b_i} - \frac{1}{p}} \right] \leqslant \prod_{p\mid \fprod{\boldsymbol{d}}}\frac{2}{p},
