which is $\ll K^{2KJ}$ by \cref{lem:trivialbound}. Plugging this into \cref{lem:useflst}, the corollary follows.

\label{def:repeatedsingle}
Let $\boldsymbol{d}\in \mathbf{D}_{\!R}$. We say that an index $(i,j)\in \sinterval{R}\times\sinterval{J}$ is \emph{single} if $\pcomp{i}{j}^2\nmid \fprod{\boldsymbol{d}}$, i.e.~the prime $\pcomp{i}{j}$ does not appear at any index other than $(i,j)$.

Given $\mathcal{S} \subset \sinterval{R}\times\sinterval{J}$, we let $\mathbf{D}^{\mathcal{S}}_{\!R}$ be the set of all $\boldsymbol{d}\in \mathbf{D}_{\!R}$ whose set of single indices is $\mathcal{S}$.

\label{lem:manip}
