Let $T := \big\lfloor \tfrac16 K^{1/2}/J\big\rfloor$.
By \cref{lem:badanalysis}, we know that every $\boldsymbol{d}\in \mathbf{D}^{\mathcal{S}}_{\!K}$ with $|{\mathcal{S}_{\mathrm{bad}}(\boldsymbol{d})}| >K^{1/2}$ satisfies a triangular system of complexity $(T; 1, 0)$. By \cref{lem:constraints}, we deduce that
